  "question": {
    "text": "A Carnot engine operating between two reservoirs has efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. When the temperature of cold reservoir raised by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>, its efficiency decreases to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>, if the temperature of hot reservoir is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>99</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi></math>, will be",
