  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A carnot engine works between two reservoirs, one hot reservoir and one cold reservoir.</p><p>The absolute temperature&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mfenced></math>&nbsp;of the hot reservoir can be calculated as follows-</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>99</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi>C</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>99</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>273</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>372</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>The formula to calculate the efficiency&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>&#951;</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;of the engine is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;is the temperature of the cold reservoir.</p><p>Substituting&nbsp;the values of the known parameters in&nbsp;equation (1), we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>372</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>248</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>The new efficiency of the engine&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Substituting&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;and the known values of the temperatures into equation (2), we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnspacing=\"0px\" columnalign=\"right center left\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd/><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd/><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>248</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>62</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd/><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>310</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>248</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd/><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>62</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>K</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p>",
